cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "TADA-Wiki: Best practice for sharing analytical code"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Edward
    name-particle: R.
    family-names: Ivimey-Cook
    email: e.ivimeycook@gmail.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4910-0443"
repository-code: "https://github.com/EIvimeyCook/TADA-Wiki"
abstract: >-
  A bookdown wiki on best practice for sharing analytical code, built around the
  TADA guidelines (Transferable, Available, Documented, Annotated). Covers
  data-sharing basics, metadata and README requirements, code and data licences,
  repository choice, the SORTEE guidelines for data and code quality control,
  and code review.
keywords:
  - open code
  - code sharing
  - reproducibility
  - research transparency
  - FAIR principles
  - metadata
  - code review
  - open science
